# Baked into the mobile bundle by `vite build --mode mobile` (build:mobile). Holds only
# the public API origin — no secrets — so it is committed, unlike .env/.env.local.
#
# The Hostinger VPS, which is where the platform lives (2026-08 move); Render and Vercel
# are retired at cutover, so a phone built against Render is a phone that stops working on
# a date nobody will remember. Installed apps keep whatever URL they were built with, so
# this file is the one that decides which server every sideloaded copy talks to.
#
# **The `/api` suffix is load-bearing.** On the VPS one origin serves both: Traefik routes
# `PathPrefix(/api)` to the API container and strips the prefix before the API sees it,
# everything else falls through to the SPA. The client composes `${API_BASE_URL}${path}`,
# so this plus `/auth/sign-in` reaches the API correctly. Point this at the bare hostname
# and every request lands on the SPA and 404s instead.
#
# The browser SPA does NOT use this file: it is built with VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api by
# docker-compose.prod.yml, same origin, no absolute host. Only the phones need one.
#
# Still to change: burgers.srv1928986.hstgr.cloud is the hostname Hostinger issued the
# box, not the client's own domain. Settle that domain before any store release — a store
# build cannot be repointed afterwards without every user reinstalling.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://burgers.srv1928986.hstgr.cloud/api
